8
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.430
Examples of trigger word systems
include the Amazon Echo,

9
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.981
which is woken up with the word Alexa,

10
00:00:29.981 --> 00:00:34.529
the Baidu DuerOS powered devices
woken up with the phrase xiaodunihao,

11
00:00:34.529 --> 00:00:40.240
Apple Siri working up with hey, Siri, and
Google Home woken up with okay, Google.

12
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.005
So it's thanks to trigger word
detection that if you have, say,

13
00:00:44.005 --> 00:00:48.045
an Amazon Echo in your living room,
you can walk in your living room and

14
00:00:48.045 --> 00:00:50.108
just say, Alexa, what time is it?

15
00:00:50.108 --> 00:00:56.140
And have it wake up or be triggered by the
word Alexa and answer your voice query.

16
00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.745
So if you can build a trigger word
detection system, maybe you can make your

17
00:01:00.745 --> 00:01:04.940
computer do something by telling it,
computer, activate.

18
00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.331
One of my friends also
worked on turning on and

19
00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:13.350
off a particular lamp using a trigger
